1
00:00:01,209 --> 00:00:03,711
- "Previously on The mentalist..."
- No!

2
00:00:08,341 --> 00:00:09,884
"We believe the assailant
is the same person"

3
00:00:10,092 --> 00:00:11,844
"that killed attorney Osvaldo Ardiles"

4
00:00:12,094 --> 00:00:15,056
"and former California Bureau
of Investigation agent J.J. Laroche."

5
00:00:15,181 --> 00:00:16,224
Good to see you, guys.

6
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:18,226
Just got word that the FBI
has officially hired you

7
00:00:18,351 --> 00:00:19,393
as consultants for the case.

8
00:00:19,519 --> 00:00:21,187
You're the ones who first found out
we were being tracked.

9
00:00:21,312 --> 00:00:22,939
You know this case
better than anybody.

10
00:00:23,189 --> 00:00:26,400
- Anything on the other seven suspects?
- A few leads. No breakthroughs.

11
00:00:26,609 --> 00:00:28,236
Which leaves us with Haibach.

12
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:44,585
Hey. I fell asleep.

13
00:00:44,752 --> 00:00:46,337
Oh, I'm sorry.
I just wanted to check in.

14
00:00:46,462 --> 00:00:47,672
I'm out having
a drink with the guys.

15
00:00:48,005 --> 00:00:49,048
What happened with Hutten?

16
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:50,967
It's not him.
I'll explain later.

17
00:00:51,634 --> 00:00:52,677
You go back to bed.

18
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,679
- You having fun?
- Yeah. Yeah, I am.

19
00:00:54,971 --> 00:00:56,889
- I'm glad. It's good for you.
- Thank you.

20
00:00:58,057 --> 00:01:00,393
- "I love you, babe. You know that, right?"
- I love you, too.

21
00:01:00,851 --> 00:01:02,853
- Okay, I'll see you soon.
- Good night.

22
00:01:45,021 --> 00:01:46,314
Well, she agreed with you.

23
00:01:46,981 --> 00:01:48,941
She said I should be out having
a drink with you guys

24
00:01:49,066 --> 00:01:50,192
said it would be good for me.

25
00:01:50,318 --> 00:01:52,862
- She's a smart woman.
- Yeah. Yeah, she is.

26
00:01:53,154 --> 00:01:54,530
I'm a lucky man.
She's the best.

27
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:56,782
A price above rubies.

28
00:01:57,366 --> 00:01:58,868
- To Grace.
- To Grace. Thank you.

29
00:02:02,121 --> 00:02:04,165
You know, Grace and I, we, uh...

30
00:02:05,291 --> 00:02:07,835
Oh, we always thought
that you and Lisbon would...

31
00:02:08,127 --> 00:02:09,170
you know, get together.

32
00:02:10,546 --> 00:02:13,007
- Jane and Lisbon... yeah, right.
- I'm just saying.

33
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:14,717
Remember when
you bought her a pony?

34
00:02:15,676 --> 00:02:17,928
Yes, I do.
I do remember that.

35
00:02:18,054 --> 00:02:19,096
I wonder what happened to it.

36
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:21,724
Okay, two more lone stars
and a club soda.

37
00:02:21,932 --> 00:02:24,185
And the man at the pool table
wants another game with you.

38
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:25,770
Well, can't he see
I'm here with my friends?

39
00:02:25,895 --> 00:02:28,898
He seemed pretty determined
said he'd make it double or nothing.

40
00:02:29,607 --> 00:02:30,650
Go and take the man's money.

41
00:02:31,817 --> 00:02:32,860
I got to get back to my wife.

42
00:02:32,985 --> 00:02:34,028
It's been a pleasure.

43
00:02:34,153 --> 00:02:35,696
- Good night. Wish me luck.
- Good luck.

44
00:02:37,114 --> 00:02:38,157
Let's get something to eat.

45
00:02:38,282 --> 00:02:39,492
Yeah, I think I saw
a drive-through on the way over.

46
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:40,785
They had chimichangas.

47
00:02:41,577 --> 00:02:42,620
Same old Rigsby.

48
00:02:57,093 --> 00:02:58,719
"You ever thought about coming
to work at the FBI?"

49
00:02:59,345 --> 00:03:00,388
"You kidding me?"

50
00:03:00,763 --> 00:03:02,390
"Been daydreaming about it
for the past six months."

51
00:03:03,974 --> 00:03:05,017
So why not join?

52
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:08,813
- You think they'd have me?
- I know they would.

53
00:03:09,855 --> 00:03:11,273
Abbott's the one
that wanted me to ask you...

54
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:12,441
Both of you, actually.

55
00:03:12,608 --> 00:03:14,110
Really? Both of us?

56
00:03:15,611 --> 00:03:16,654
I don't know.

57
00:03:17,071 --> 00:03:18,948
It's a pretty 24/7 type of gig.

58
00:03:19,532 --> 00:03:20,825
Someone's got to look
after the kids.

59
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:23,536
You should talk about it with Grace.
The offer's there.

60
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:25,496
Nice. Okay.

61
00:03:26,497 --> 00:03:27,998
Well, you want to come up for a drink
discuss it with Grace?

62
00:03:28,624 --> 00:03:30,960
No. Best you two
talk about it alone.

63
00:03:31,627 --> 00:03:33,421
Right. Yeah,
you're probably right.

64
00:03:35,881 --> 00:03:37,007
Hey. Why's the door to your room open?

65
00:03:38,884 --> 00:03:39,927
I don't know.

66
00:03:55,985 --> 00:03:57,027
Grace?

67
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:03,617
Grace?

68
00:04:06,871 --> 00:04:08,581
Grace? Grace?!

69
00:04:16,338 --> 00:04:18,507
Keys are still on the table.
So is her wallet.

70
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:21,927
There's a perfectly reasonable
explanation for this, right?

71
00:04:22,219 --> 00:04:23,929
- Please tell me there's one.
- Don't jump to conclusions.

72
00:04:24,054 --> 00:04:25,347
- What are you doing?
- Calling her cell.

73
00:04:39,987 --> 00:04:41,113
Where are you, Grace?

74
00:05:10,808 --> 00:05:11,850
Hello?

75
00:05:16,355 --> 00:05:17,397
Is anybody there?

76
00:05:20,859 --> 00:05:21,902
Hello!

77
00:05:22,861 --> 00:05:25,113
{\an8}Rigsby and Jane are with a team
combing through the motel room

78
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:26,323
{\an8}but we've got nothing yet.

79
00:05:26,448 --> 00:05:27,658
{\an8}there's about a thousand
different fingerprints

80
00:05:27,783 --> 00:05:29,117
{\an8}and DNA
all over everything.

81
00:05:29,409 --> 00:05:30,702
{\an8}I hate hotel rooms.

82
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,497
{\an8}How's Wylie doing
with the camera footage

83
00:05:33,622 --> 00:05:34,665
{\an8}that we pulled
from around town?

84
00:05:35,249 --> 00:05:37,125
He's traced her whereabouts
before she got to the motel.

85
00:05:37,793 --> 00:05:38,836
Anything useful?

86
00:05:39,711 --> 00:05:40,963
- No.
- Well, what else?

87
00:05:41,672 --> 00:05:43,590
{\an8}An S.U.V. leaving the area
of the motel

88
00:05:43,715 --> 00:05:46,093
{\an8}at the estimated time
of Grace Van Pelt's abduction.

89
00:05:47,469 --> 00:05:49,054
Was he able to get
a license plate from it?

90
00:05:49,263 --> 00:05:50,305
No.

91
00:05:55,936 --> 00:05:57,855
{\an8}All right, people, listen up.

92
00:05:59,731 --> 00:06:03,360
{\an8}We already know our prime suspect...
Richard Haibach.

93
00:06:04,236 --> 00:06:06,446
We were already looking at him
for the murders

94
00:06:06,613 --> 00:06:10,617
{\an8}of ex-CBI agent J.J. Laroche
and D.A. Osvaldo Ardiles.

95
00:06:11,285 --> 00:06:13,829
{\an8}Now Grace Van Pelt is gone.
Where?

96
00:06:14,663 --> 00:06:15,706
{\an8}We don't know.

97
00:06:16,164 --> 00:06:18,625
But we're assuming
that Haibach is responsible.

98
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:19,793
Excuse me, agent Abbott?

99
00:06:21,003 --> 00:06:23,297
We got a bolo out.
We alerted the media.

100
00:06:23,630 --> 00:06:26,633
{\an8}But Haibach has already slipped
our tail In Colorado.

101
00:06:27,718 --> 00:06:30,095
{\an8}He's in the wind.
He knows we're coming after him.

102
00:06:30,220 --> 00:06:31,805
{\an8}And he will not be easy to find.

103
00:06:32,014 --> 00:06:33,348
{\an8}Agent Abbott, there's someone
to see you.

104
00:06:33,932 --> 00:06:36,101
{\an8}But find him we will.

105
00:06:37,102 --> 00:06:41,106
{\an8}Whatever it takes, people.
Failure is not an option here.

106
00:06:42,149 --> 00:06:43,567
{\an8}Find Richard Haibach.

107
00:06:49,031 --> 00:06:50,657
Agent Wylie, what do you need?

108
00:06:50,866 --> 00:06:53,452
{\an8}Well, there's a... There's a man
who came to reception downstairs.

109
00:06:53,577 --> 00:06:55,454
- An agent's bringing him up.
- So?

110
00:06:55,704 --> 00:06:57,122
{\an8}The man says
he's Richard Haibach.

111
00:07:04,922 --> 00:07:06,089
Go get Jane back here now.

112
00:07:21,188 --> 00:07:22,230
{\an8}Hello?!

113
00:07:26,777 --> 00:07:27,945
{\an8}Is anybody here?!

114
00:08:07,776 --> 00:08:09,611
{\an8}Hello, agent Lisbon, Mr. Jane.

115
00:08:10,278 --> 00:08:11,321
Sit down, please.

116
00:08:11,446 --> 00:08:12,489
Why are you here,
Mr. Haibach?

117
00:08:13,865 --> 00:08:14,908
Is that some kind of joke?

118
00:08:16,118 --> 00:08:17,160
I've been in fear of my life

119
00:08:17,285 --> 00:08:18,704
since I learned you were
stalking me again.

120
00:08:19,621 --> 00:08:21,415
We're not stalking you,
Mr. Haibach.

121
00:08:21,999 --> 00:08:24,418
I knew the moment you started
asking questions about me

122
00:08:24,543 --> 00:08:26,545
behind my back
to people at my job

123
00:08:26,837 --> 00:08:28,005
that you were out to get me.

124
00:08:28,296 --> 00:08:29,923
I already apologized
to you for that.

125
00:08:30,507 --> 00:08:31,550
Oh, you apologized

126
00:08:31,758 --> 00:08:33,427
but that didn't stop
your plotting, did it?

127
00:08:33,969 --> 00:08:35,345
We just had
a few questions for you.

128
00:08:35,679 --> 00:08:38,515
Really? So I'm not
your number-one suspect?

129
00:08:39,808 --> 00:08:40,851
This a game?

130
00:08:41,768 --> 00:08:43,061
No game, Mr. Jane.

131
00:08:43,895 --> 00:08:46,481
I am, as I said,
in fear for my life.

132
00:08:46,773 --> 00:08:47,899
Think about what you're doing.

133
00:08:49,317 --> 00:08:50,902
These are people
I care a lot about.

134
00:08:52,112 --> 00:08:53,155
Yes or no...

135
00:08:53,822 --> 00:08:56,158
A warrant has been issued
for my arrest, hasn't it?

136
00:08:56,366 --> 00:08:58,785
- How did you know about that?
- So one has.

137
00:08:59,745 --> 00:09:01,288
I call that an execution order

138
00:09:01,830 --> 00:09:04,207
a license to shoot me down
in the street like a dog.

139
00:09:05,250 --> 00:09:08,086
So I'm here to prove my innocence
beyond any shadow of a doubt.

140
00:09:08,879 --> 00:09:09,921
Do you have any knowledge

141
00:09:10,047 --> 00:09:11,339
as to what's happened
to Grace Van Pelt?

142
00:09:12,966 --> 00:09:14,760
No. I don't.

143
00:09:15,385 --> 00:09:18,430
- How could I?
- Take a guess...for fun.

144
00:09:19,264 --> 00:09:20,307
Okay. Sure.

145
00:09:21,850 --> 00:09:25,020
I can make plenty of guesses
but that's all it is... guesses.

146
00:09:26,104 --> 00:09:27,147
But...

147
00:09:28,106 --> 00:09:29,149
Let's see.

148
00:09:30,192 --> 00:09:32,694
I'd guess she was...

149
00:09:33,570 --> 00:09:36,364
Somewhere far away,
out of the reach of your help

150
00:09:36,865 --> 00:09:38,033
out of the reach
of anyone's help...

151
00:09:39,159 --> 00:09:40,702
alone and trapped...

152
00:09:41,661 --> 00:09:42,704
with time running out...

153
00:09:44,039 --> 00:09:45,165
if I were to guess, I mean.

154
00:09:47,959 --> 00:09:49,961
Showing up like this
is a bad sign.

155
00:09:50,754 --> 00:09:53,048
90% of the time, it means
the victim's already dead.

156
00:09:53,215 --> 00:09:55,133
Well, I don't see any reason
to jump to conclusions.

157
00:09:55,258 --> 00:09:57,427
You've been through the Quantico
profiling courses, too.

158
00:09:58,053 --> 00:10:00,972
His performative aspect suggests
that he's already killed her.

159
00:10:01,098 --> 00:10:02,849
He's just here to gloat
when we find the body.

160
00:10:08,021 --> 00:10:09,064
Where's my wife?!

161
00:10:09,481 --> 00:10:10,524
Rigsby!

162
00:10:10,649 --> 00:10:11,691
What have you done with her?!

163
00:10:11,817 --> 00:10:12,859
Come on, please.

164
00:10:12,984 --> 00:10:14,402
If you hurt her, I'll kill you!
You're an animal!

165
00:10:14,611 --> 00:10:17,447
Hurt her?! Look at me!
What about me?!

166
00:10:17,572 --> 00:10:18,615
- I'll kill you!
- No!

167
00:10:19,116 --> 00:10:20,200
Stop! Not here!

168
00:10:20,450 --> 00:10:24,704
I was tortured because you people
thought I deserved it and I did nothing!

169
00:10:25,539 --> 00:10:26,581
I did nothing!

170
00:10:26,706 --> 00:10:28,625
My thumb was cut off
because of you!

171
00:10:28,750 --> 00:10:31,253
- You people are the animals!
- Sit down, Mr. Haibach.

172
00:10:46,601 --> 00:10:47,644
Okay, Rigsby, Listen.

173
00:10:47,894 --> 00:10:50,355
I understand how you're feeling
right now. Believe me.

174
00:10:50,647 --> 00:10:53,608
But you are a father and you have
children you need to see grow up.

175
00:10:54,568 --> 00:10:57,445
- Besides, I think she's still alive.
- You do?

176
00:10:57,696 --> 00:10:58,738
Yes.

177
00:10:59,364 --> 00:11:01,324
Haibach's revenge plan
was disrupted by Grace

178
00:11:01,449 --> 00:11:02,826
when she broke
his phone hacks up.

179
00:11:03,702 --> 00:11:04,870
He realized then

180
00:11:05,453 --> 00:11:07,956
that it was only a matter of time
before we tracked him down.

181
00:11:08,707 --> 00:11:11,251
This is him making
the best of the situation.

182
00:11:11,459 --> 00:11:12,502
Then why did he come here?

183
00:11:12,878 --> 00:11:14,880
To gloat and watch us squirm.

184
00:11:15,797 --> 00:11:18,091
And he plans to make us
let him go when he's done.

185
00:11:18,592 --> 00:11:19,676
We won't let him
get away with it.

186
00:12:19,527 --> 00:12:22,906
I wonder if you'd mind telling us

187
00:12:23,031 --> 00:12:24,991
where you've been
for the last 24 hours.

188
00:12:26,076 --> 00:12:28,620
Do you own an S.U.V....
Maybe gray?

189
00:12:28,870 --> 00:12:29,913
No, I don't.

190
00:12:30,455 --> 00:12:36,419
But this is a video of me
on the bus from Denver to Austin.

191
00:12:38,505 --> 00:12:39,714
This is my bus ticket.

192
00:12:42,217 --> 00:12:43,260
And these are the names

193
00:12:43,385 --> 00:12:45,387
of three of the other passengers
on the bus and the bus driver.

194
00:12:45,512 --> 00:12:47,764
They can confirm I was on the bus
during the entire trip.

195
00:12:48,890 --> 00:12:50,850
And in this envelope

196
00:12:51,184 --> 00:12:53,770
is everything you need to know
about my whereabouts

197
00:12:53,937 --> 00:12:56,273
during the time of the murders
of Osvaldo Ardiles

198
00:12:56,398 --> 00:12:57,440
and J.J. Laroche.

199
00:12:57,565 --> 00:12:59,150
It's tabulated and cross-referenced.

200
00:13:00,318 --> 00:13:04,614
Now, my attorney is scheduled
to arrive, well, anytime now.

201
00:13:06,908 --> 00:13:09,911
Okay, Haibach's attorney
is gonna be here at any second

202
00:13:10,453 --> 00:13:11,955
and we have no reason
to hold him.

203
00:13:12,330 --> 00:13:13,373
This is his alibi.

204
00:13:14,416 --> 00:13:17,794
I want it turned inside out
and torn apart.

205
00:13:17,919 --> 00:13:19,587
Find the holes
and see where they lead.

206
00:13:21,381 --> 00:13:23,049
In any event,
the evidence suggests

207
00:13:23,174 --> 00:13:25,218
that Haibach is working
with an accomplice.

208
00:13:26,177 --> 00:13:27,220
Find out who that is...

209
00:13:27,679 --> 00:13:29,848
Somebody he hangs out with
at work

210
00:13:30,181 --> 00:13:32,100
somebody that he met
on the internet

211
00:13:33,018 --> 00:13:35,061
old friend, new friend.

212
00:13:35,437 --> 00:13:37,397
Find the accomplice.

213
00:13:37,897 --> 00:13:39,941
And do it quickly.
We don't have the luxury of time.

214
00:13:54,789 --> 00:13:55,832
Oh, damn it.

215
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:14,976
Okay, here's the bus route
from Denver to Austin.

216
00:14:15,435 --> 00:14:16,478
How many miles is that?

217
00:14:16,811 --> 00:14:19,606
Um... let me see.

218
00:14:22,609 --> 00:14:25,153
It's a little over
916 miles.

219
00:14:26,279 --> 00:14:27,989
"Daddy, are you coming home?"

220
00:14:30,075 --> 00:14:31,618
Not for a little while longer, buddy.

221
00:14:32,702 --> 00:14:34,287
You're having a good time
with your mom, though, right?

222
00:14:34,454 --> 00:14:36,623
"I guess. She works a lot."

223
00:14:37,582 --> 00:14:38,750
"Is Grace there?"

224
00:14:40,502 --> 00:14:43,380
No. She's... she's not here right now.

225
00:14:44,172 --> 00:14:46,966
"She always tells me a story
before my nap."

226
00:14:47,384 --> 00:14:48,426
A story?

227
00:14:48,593 --> 00:14:51,096
"About a nice bull
who has to go to the bull fight."

228
00:14:51,262 --> 00:14:54,015
Ferdinand.
Well, he gets to go home.

229
00:14:54,391 --> 00:14:56,684
- "And smell the flowers."
- Yeah.

230
00:14:57,644 --> 00:15:00,605
And he's very happy,
sitting under a big tree.

231
00:15:00,939 --> 00:15:01,981
"Yeah."

232
00:15:02,690 --> 00:15:05,735
Okay, look, I...
I have to go, buddy.

233
00:15:06,903 --> 00:15:09,697
We'll speak very soon, okay?
Daddy loves you.

234
00:15:10,323 --> 00:15:13,493
- "Love you, too. Bye, dad."
- Bye, son.

235
00:15:19,290 --> 00:15:20,333
Excuse me.

236
00:15:25,088 --> 00:15:26,131
Hey.

237
00:15:29,426 --> 00:15:30,885
Haibach's lawyer is here.

238
00:15:31,511 --> 00:15:33,888
Abbott's gonna try and stall her
for as long as he can

239
00:15:34,055 --> 00:15:36,766
but we're probably
gonna have to let Haibach go.

240
00:15:37,684 --> 00:15:39,978
We don't have enough concrete
evidence to hold him on.

241
00:15:44,983 --> 00:15:46,025
Okay.

242
00:16:01,166 --> 00:16:03,543
Jane, whatever it takes.

243
00:16:04,169 --> 00:16:06,504
Please. I'm begging you.
We have to get Grace back.

244
00:16:14,012 --> 00:16:15,138
I should have been contacted

245
00:16:15,263 --> 00:16:17,640
the moment my client
arrived at your offices.

246
00:16:17,807 --> 00:16:20,435
Well, he came
on his own volition.

247
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:21,853
We simply met him
as he asked.

248
00:16:22,395 --> 00:16:24,731
Well, I'd like to speak to my client alone.

249
00:16:26,191 --> 00:16:29,027
Look at me. You know me.
You know what I am capable of.

250
00:16:29,277 --> 00:16:31,446
So if you have done anything
to Grace Van Pelt

251
00:16:31,654 --> 00:16:32,780
I am gonna make you pay.

252
00:16:32,906 --> 00:16:35,074
Excuse me. The law says you
can't just charge in here...

253
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,242
Oh, don't you worry
about the law.

254
00:16:36,367 --> 00:16:37,452
You need to worry
about me.

255
00:16:37,577 --> 00:16:38,620
Is this man completely insane?

256
00:16:38,745 --> 00:16:41,706
And no matter where you go
I will find you, and I will make you pay.

257
00:16:41,831 --> 00:16:44,459
Agent Abbott, in all my years,
I have never witnessed...

258
00:16:44,584 --> 00:16:45,877
- All right, that's enough, Jane.
- Okay.

259
00:16:46,544 --> 00:16:48,922
See, what you don't understand
about me, Rich is I don't care.

260
00:16:49,214 --> 00:16:50,256
I've got nothing to lose.

261
00:16:50,381 --> 00:16:51,925
I've been playing
with the house money for years.

262
00:16:52,217 --> 00:16:54,719
And if I go to prison for what
I do to you, I don't care.

263
00:16:54,844 --> 00:16:56,804
- Okay, come on. That's enough.
- If your friend dies, it's your fault.

264
00:16:56,930 --> 00:16:58,056
- That's enough.
- You can't blame me!

265
00:16:58,890 --> 00:17:00,808
I had nothing to do with it...
Nothing at all!

266
00:17:01,392 --> 00:17:04,979
- What in the hell were you doing?
- The unexpected.

267
00:17:05,104 --> 00:17:06,147
Yeah, it was that.

268
00:17:06,272 --> 00:17:08,691
Well, we want Haibach
out of his comfort zone

269
00:17:09,275 --> 00:17:10,944
so we push him
to make a mistake.

270
00:17:12,237 --> 00:17:15,615
Okay, now, we both know I give
you a lot of latitude

271
00:17:15,990 --> 00:17:18,326
but you just criminally
threatened a suspect

272
00:17:18,451 --> 00:17:20,119
in front of his lawyer
on video.

273
00:17:20,453 --> 00:17:21,788
It's admissible in court.

274
00:17:22,372 --> 00:17:25,041
He came here with a plan,
and we don't know what that plan is

275
00:17:25,166 --> 00:17:26,209
but he does.

276
00:17:26,334 --> 00:17:27,752
So he knows the pattern
in advance.

277
00:17:28,670 --> 00:17:30,672
We need to break
that pattern.

278
00:18:27,284 --> 00:18:28,327
Do you have a minute?

279
00:18:29,453 --> 00:18:31,747
Just waiting for my client.
Knock yourself out.

280
00:18:33,065 --> 00:18:34,775
We just need
a little more time.

281
00:18:36,611 --> 00:18:37,653
Really?

282
00:18:38,321 --> 00:18:40,156
My firm is already in the process
of getting

283
00:18:40,281 --> 00:18:42,992
the depositions of the bus's
passengers and the driver.

284
00:18:43,618 --> 00:18:45,119
We'll have them all
by this evening.

285
00:18:46,245 --> 00:18:49,957
Richard Haibach's whereabouts
during the abduction of your associate

286
00:18:50,082 --> 00:18:52,209
can be stated with absolute certainty.

287
00:18:54,253 --> 00:18:55,838
You have no reason
to hold my client.

288
00:18:56,422 --> 00:18:59,258
Not yet, but the reason is there.

289
00:19:00,384 --> 00:19:01,886
Now, even you
have to see that.

290
00:19:02,845 --> 00:19:04,513
He took her.
We all know that he did.

291
00:19:05,431 --> 00:19:06,474
Then prove it.

292
00:19:07,016 --> 00:19:08,768
Otherwise, you have to let my client go.

293
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:10,811
That's the way the law works.

294
00:19:10,936 --> 00:19:13,397
He'll kill her if we let him go,
if he hasn't already.

295
00:19:13,522 --> 00:19:14,565
Do you realize that?

296
00:19:14,690 --> 00:19:16,984
Look, don't try
and make me feel guilty.

297
00:19:17,485 --> 00:19:18,861
I've been doing this
a long time

298
00:19:18,986 --> 00:19:21,656
and my job as a lawyer
is to defend my client.

299
00:19:22,031 --> 00:19:23,866
That's why people pay me.

300
00:19:24,450 --> 00:19:26,827
So you can give me
whatever sob story you want

301
00:19:26,952 --> 00:19:28,537
but we both know
you've got nothing.

302
00:19:28,704 --> 00:19:30,665
Whatever happens
is on your head.

303
00:19:31,499 --> 00:19:36,337
That is inaccurate
unprofessional, and disrespectful.

304
00:19:36,545 --> 00:19:38,839
I'm doing my job.
Don't make me do yours.

305
00:19:43,678 --> 00:19:44,720
Hello?!

306
00:19:47,223 --> 00:19:48,265
Is anybody out here?!

307
00:19:50,226 --> 00:19:51,519
Anybody out here?!

308
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:19,630
Hey. Hey.

309
00:20:20,297 --> 00:20:21,340
Hey!

310
00:20:22,466 --> 00:20:23,509
Hey.

311
00:20:26,220 --> 00:20:27,263
Are you okay?

312
00:20:27,388 --> 00:20:29,223
- Do you have a phone? I just...
- Well, look, were you in an accident?

313
00:20:29,348 --> 00:20:30,683
just need a phone.
Please, do you have a phone?

314
00:20:30,808 --> 00:20:32,601
Okay, okay, okay.
Okay, here. Here it is.

315
00:20:33,102 --> 00:20:34,145
Thank you.

316
00:20:37,690 --> 00:20:38,774
- Is there coverage?
- I don't know.

317
00:20:38,899 --> 00:20:39,942
It's kind of spotty out here.

318
00:20:40,067 --> 00:20:41,444
You're half-frozen.
Where's your car?

319
00:20:41,819 --> 00:20:42,862
Where's the police station?

320
00:20:43,612 --> 00:20:46,323
Taos, I guess.
That's 45 minutes north of here.

321
00:20:46,532 --> 00:20:48,284
Or there's a ranger station
about a half an hour south.

322
00:20:48,409 --> 00:20:49,452
Where's the nearest phone?

323
00:20:49,910 --> 00:20:51,036
Well, my cabin, I guess.

324
00:20:51,579 --> 00:20:53,205
Okay, okay.
I need you to take me there.

325
00:20:53,330 --> 00:20:54,665
Can you take me there? It's important.
Just take me there right now.

326
00:20:54,874 --> 00:20:56,375
Yeah, yeah. All right.
Get in, get in, get in.

327
00:20:56,959 --> 00:20:58,002
Okay.

328
00:20:59,712 --> 00:21:00,755
Oh, you must be frozen.

329
00:21:01,088 --> 00:21:02,131
Yeah.

330
00:21:06,719 --> 00:21:09,847
I've looked into Haibach's known
associates. It's a short list.

331
00:21:10,055 --> 00:21:12,391
He was a loner at work
and in his private life.

332
00:21:12,767 --> 00:21:15,936
He's got an older sister named Hazel
that I haven't been able to contact.

333
00:21:16,103 --> 00:21:18,397
I sent local P.D. to check her address.
Should be hearing soon.

334
00:21:18,647 --> 00:21:20,983
Dubin knows we don't have enough
to charge Haibach.

335
00:21:21,817 --> 00:21:22,860
We have to let him walk.

336
00:21:25,154 --> 00:21:26,197
I'll tell Rigsby.

337
00:21:26,322 --> 00:21:27,364
Keep him together, okay?

338
00:21:31,035 --> 00:21:32,787
You think if I talk
to this lawyer woman to woman

339
00:21:32,912 --> 00:21:34,455
it would have any effect?

340
00:21:35,456 --> 00:21:36,540
Don't waste your time.

341
00:21:45,341 --> 00:21:47,760
Okay, here we are.
Home sweet home.

342
00:21:49,804 --> 00:21:51,013
Come on, darling,
let's get you inside.

343
00:21:51,138 --> 00:21:53,432
- Get you something warm.
- Okay. Thanks.

344
00:22:05,611 --> 00:22:07,863
Okay, now, mind those steps,
'cause those are slippery.

345
00:22:14,036 --> 00:22:15,955
Hey, shut the door behind you.
Don't let the heat out.

346
00:22:16,413 --> 00:22:17,748
Phone's in the bedroom.
I'll go get it.

347
00:22:21,460 --> 00:22:24,296
- No electricity, huh?
- Oh, lord. Bless your heart. No.

348
00:22:24,421 --> 00:22:25,631
The poles don't come out this far.

349
00:22:26,882 --> 00:22:29,176
- Then how do you have a phone?
- I don't.

350
00:22:30,344 --> 00:22:31,387
I lied.

351
00:22:51,323 --> 00:22:54,159
Okay, kids, time's up.
Put your pencils down.

352
00:22:55,202 --> 00:22:56,787
We're processing
your client right now.

353
00:22:57,621 --> 00:22:59,164
I'll tell my car to pull around.

354
00:23:04,587 --> 00:23:06,839
Okay, that's right.
Pull it tight.

355
00:23:08,132 --> 00:23:09,174
Use your teeth.

356
00:23:14,972 --> 00:23:16,015
Okay.

357
00:23:16,849 --> 00:23:18,350
So you just stay here
and you don't cause trouble.

358
00:23:18,475 --> 00:23:19,977
Richard's gonna know what to do
with you when he gets here.

359
00:23:21,478 --> 00:23:22,980
Please, do you have
anything hot to drink?

360
00:23:27,359 --> 00:23:28,444
I got some coffee
I can heat up.

361
00:23:29,445 --> 00:23:31,030
That'd be great. Thanks.

362
00:23:31,572 --> 00:23:32,615
And no tricks.

363
00:23:33,699 --> 00:23:34,742
No tricks.

364
00:23:44,627 --> 00:23:45,920
My name's Grace,
by the way.

365
00:23:46,462 --> 00:23:48,422
Don't you try and make friends,
'cause I'm not stupid.

366
00:23:48,923 --> 00:23:50,925
Okay. Sorry.

367
00:24:00,142 --> 00:24:01,602
Richard's your brother,
isn't he?

368
00:24:07,441 --> 00:24:08,817
It was just the two of you,
wasn't it?

369
00:24:09,860 --> 00:24:11,403
- No other sisters or brothers?
- Yep.

370
00:24:15,282 --> 00:24:17,660
- You're older?
- Three years.

371
00:24:23,582 --> 00:24:25,584
Something happened
when you were kids, didn't it?

372
00:24:27,294 --> 00:24:28,337
Something bad.

373
00:24:31,757 --> 00:24:34,843
Richard had it
so hard growing up.

374
00:24:36,345 --> 00:24:37,513
You people
didn't understand that.

375
00:24:38,973 --> 00:24:40,015
It wasn't his fault.

376
00:24:41,475 --> 00:24:42,518
What was so hard?

377
00:24:44,728 --> 00:24:48,399
Our mother run away
left us both with a drunk.

378
00:24:49,608 --> 00:24:50,985
And he did things
to Richard.

379
00:24:53,946 --> 00:24:54,989
Things he shouldn't have.

380
00:24:58,951 --> 00:24:59,994
Wasn't his fault.

381
00:25:02,204 --> 00:25:03,247
I didn't protect him.

382
00:25:05,332 --> 00:25:07,960
His big sister...
Didn't protect him.

383
00:25:09,378 --> 00:25:11,380
You were just a little girl.
It's not your fault.

384
00:25:11,964 --> 00:25:13,257
Don't you pretend sympathy.

385
00:25:14,508 --> 00:25:17,594
You people are bad as my father...
What you did to Richard.

386
00:25:18,929 --> 00:25:21,682
He wasn't hurting nobody,
but you pushed and you pushed.

387
00:25:22,182 --> 00:25:24,268
And now, miss cutie pie,
it is you who's gonna be hurt.

388
00:25:25,144 --> 00:25:26,186
'cause that's only fair.

389
00:25:33,819 --> 00:25:35,904
"The next step will be
taking the FBI to court."

390
00:25:36,280 --> 00:25:38,407
"We have grounds
for a strong suit."

391
00:25:39,992 --> 00:25:41,410
Will they all lose their jobs?

392
00:25:42,411 --> 00:25:45,831
Well, sure, but there's potential
for a large settlement, as well...

393
00:25:46,665 --> 00:25:49,418
- Eight-figures large.
- I don't care about money.

394
00:25:50,252 --> 00:25:52,296
I just want to make sure
Patrick Jane suffers.

395
00:25:52,880 --> 00:25:54,465
I want him to suffer a lot.

396
00:25:58,177 --> 00:26:01,013
Hey, you missed he on-ramp.
This is the wrong way.

397
00:26:02,181 --> 00:26:04,641
No, you don't have to stop.
You can just take the next right.

398
00:26:13,275 --> 00:26:14,318
Hello, again.

399
00:26:14,568 --> 00:26:16,278
Haibach, counselor.

400
00:26:26,486 --> 00:26:28,446
Jane and Rigsby
are missing.

401
00:26:29,864 --> 00:26:33,451
We found Dubin's livery driver
locked up in a downstairs closet.

402
00:26:33,919 --> 00:26:36,838
Sir, honestly, I didn't know
anything about this.

403
00:26:37,130 --> 00:26:38,173
We had nothing
to do with it.

404
00:26:38,965 --> 00:26:40,217
But we would have,
if they asked.

405
00:26:40,675 --> 00:26:43,428
Now, I'm sure you
find that brave and noble

406
00:26:44,387 --> 00:26:45,430
but it's not.

407
00:26:45,972 --> 00:26:48,934
You're federal agents,
and I expect you to behave as such.

408
00:26:49,142 --> 00:26:50,852
Otherwise, I have no use for you.

409
00:26:52,646 --> 00:26:53,688
Now get out of my office.

410
00:27:02,030 --> 00:27:03,073
Fischer.

411
00:27:05,033 --> 00:27:07,244
Find them. Right now.

412
00:27:16,586 --> 00:27:17,629
Get out.

413
00:27:17,879 --> 00:27:18,922
Oh, you people are insane.

414
00:27:19,047 --> 00:27:20,132
You're never gonna
get away with this.

415
00:27:20,257 --> 00:27:22,926
Listen, he took my wife.
Whatever he gets, he deserves.

416
00:27:23,093 --> 00:27:24,136
Now go.

417
00:27:26,346 --> 00:27:27,389
Counselor.

418
00:27:29,516 --> 00:27:30,559
Here.

419
00:27:31,059 --> 00:27:33,019
You should probably think
about your choice of clients

420
00:27:33,145 --> 00:27:34,563
on your little walk back to Austin.

421
00:27:40,610 --> 00:27:41,653
Looks good.

422
00:28:02,883 --> 00:28:03,925
I'm a mother, you know.

423
00:28:05,385 --> 00:28:07,679
I have a baby girl.
Her name's Maddy.

424
00:28:09,097 --> 00:28:10,390
Cut it out.
I don't want to hear about it.

425
00:28:12,142 --> 00:28:13,476
We named her
after my grandmother.

426
00:28:14,102 --> 00:28:15,187
Her name's really Madeleine

427
00:28:15,312 --> 00:28:17,189
but she looks more
like a Maddy, you know?

428
00:28:19,441 --> 00:28:21,318
She shouldn't have to grow up
without a mother, should she?

429
00:28:23,486 --> 00:28:24,571
You just don't get it, do you?

430
00:28:25,030 --> 00:28:27,574
This isn't about you.
This is about me and Richard.

431
00:28:27,949 --> 00:28:30,744
Everybody has looked down on us.
It's like we were nothing.

432
00:28:31,411 --> 00:28:32,454
But now they'll see.

433
00:28:32,704 --> 00:28:34,789
Hazel and Richard are gonna
get the attention they deserve.

434
00:28:37,375 --> 00:28:38,418
Hey.

435
00:28:39,836 --> 00:28:40,879
Hey.

436
00:28:41,630 --> 00:28:42,672
Wait a minute.

437
00:28:44,216 --> 00:28:45,258
What were you just doing?

438
00:28:46,927 --> 00:28:47,969
Put your hands up.

439
00:28:49,095 --> 00:28:50,138
Put 'em up!

440
00:28:51,306 --> 00:28:52,432
Oh, you little bitch!

441
00:28:54,017 --> 00:28:56,895
You were, oh, just making all nice.

442
00:28:57,270 --> 00:29:00,774
And the whole time
you're just lying, lying, lying to me.

443
00:29:01,274 --> 00:29:02,901
Aah! Hazel, that's too tight.
You're hurting me.

444
00:29:03,068 --> 00:29:05,362
Well, that's what you deserve,
isn't it, you big liar?!

445
00:29:05,904 --> 00:29:07,614
And you know what...
when Richard gets here

446
00:29:07,864 --> 00:29:11,368
I'm gonna tell him all about this
and he's gonna be so mad.

447
00:29:11,993 --> 00:29:13,036
You know what?

448
00:29:13,328 --> 00:29:15,956
I don't want to hear
any more of your words!

449
00:29:26,424 --> 00:29:28,134
Where is she?!
Where's my wife?

450
00:29:28,260 --> 00:29:29,302
You're wasting your time.

451
00:29:31,263 --> 00:29:34,099
- Where is she?!
- I won't tell you where she is.

452
00:29:36,142 --> 00:29:37,727
You can kill me.
It won't make a difference.

453
00:29:40,939 --> 00:29:42,148
- I'm gonna die! I'm gonna die!
- Whoa, whoa.

454
00:29:42,274 --> 00:29:43,316
Does that change anything?

455
00:29:44,359 --> 00:29:46,069
No! Stop! Stop!

456
00:30:00,458 --> 00:30:02,210
Answer me.
Where is she?

457
00:30:03,378 --> 00:30:04,421
Rigsby.

458
00:30:04,713 --> 00:30:05,755
Where's my wife?!

459
00:30:05,880 --> 00:30:08,049
Whoa, Rigsby! Calm down,
calm down. Just count to 10.

460
00:30:08,466 --> 00:30:11,303
- Just count to 10. Count to 10.
- Where's my wife?

461
00:30:12,679 --> 00:30:13,722
No, we don't
want to kill him.

462
00:30:13,888 --> 00:30:15,807
We just want to make him talk.
I have a plan.

463
00:30:16,266 --> 00:30:17,684
This isn't about
one of your plans.

464
00:30:17,809 --> 00:30:20,562
See, you need to just stop
and just talk to me, okay?

465
00:30:20,687 --> 00:30:23,481
Talk to me, Rigsby.
There's another way.

466
00:30:23,982 --> 00:30:25,025
I'm gonna make him talk.

467
00:30:26,735 --> 00:30:28,194
No, Rigsby.

468
00:30:28,570 --> 00:30:31,072
No! No, Rigsby.
You don't want to do this.

469
00:30:34,492 --> 00:30:35,910
I got no time
to play games here.

470
00:30:36,369 --> 00:30:37,412
I want answers!

471
00:30:39,956 --> 00:30:42,667
Answer me!
Where's my wife?!

472
00:30:43,543 --> 00:30:44,586
Last chance!

473
00:30:47,047 --> 00:30:49,174
Okay, you need
to let me handle this.

474
00:30:49,632 --> 00:30:51,426
No, there's no time.
I have to find Grace.

475
00:30:51,801 --> 00:30:54,387
You're gonna set fire to the only person
that can tell us where she is.

476
00:30:54,512 --> 00:30:55,930
What is the point of that?

477
00:30:56,639 --> 00:30:57,682
What is that gonna prove?

478
00:30:58,183 --> 00:30:59,225
Drop something?

479
00:31:01,770 --> 00:31:02,854
- No, don't.
- Drop the flare.

480
00:31:02,979 --> 00:31:04,064
- Get rid of the flare!
- Okay, okay.

481
00:31:04,856 --> 00:31:05,899
Give me your coat.

482
00:31:07,609 --> 00:31:09,110
Put the vest in the trunk.

483
00:31:09,694 --> 00:31:11,946
You, Jane, you're gonna drive.

484
00:31:13,573 --> 00:31:14,616
Let's go.

485
00:31:15,408 --> 00:31:16,451
Easy.

486
00:31:18,161 --> 00:31:19,579
Man was curious
about his wife.

487
00:31:20,580 --> 00:31:22,207
I'm gonna satisfy
that curiosity.

488
00:31:22,374 --> 00:31:23,416
Get in.

489
00:31:37,553 --> 00:31:39,472
They found Dubin
on old highway 29.

490
00:31:40,473 --> 00:31:42,558
Maybe they're headed for hill country.
Haibach could have a place out there.

491
00:31:42,767 --> 00:31:43,851
Yeah, I don't think so.

492
00:31:44,018 --> 00:31:45,770
I've had agents searching
every inch of the state.

493
00:31:45,895 --> 00:31:47,105
I think they're out of Texas.

494
00:31:48,189 --> 00:31:49,232
I have an idea.

495
00:31:49,899 --> 00:31:52,485
Maybe. New Mexico.

496
00:31:52,735 --> 00:31:54,195
Up in the Sangre de Cristo mountains.

497
00:31:54,570 --> 00:31:55,613
Why do you think that?

498
00:31:55,738 --> 00:31:58,074
Well, I thought I'd try coming
from a different angle, you know?

499
00:31:58,199 --> 00:31:59,242
'cause everyone kept saying

500
00:31:59,367 --> 00:32:01,244
How Haibach was being
so careful and stuff.

501
00:32:01,369 --> 00:32:03,746
So first I looked into where Haibach
was born and grew up.

502
00:32:03,913 --> 00:32:04,956
Oh, let me guess...
New Mexico?

503
00:32:05,081 --> 00:32:07,875
No, but he had grandparents there
spent time there as a child.

504
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:09,585
He liked it, returned whenever he could.

505
00:32:10,086 --> 00:32:13,131
In fact, he wrote his thesis in college

506
00:32:13,256 --> 00:32:15,967
on the pueblo people culture,
which is centered in New Mexico.

507
00:32:16,217 --> 00:32:18,803
He... he didn't actually do too
well on the paper, actually...

508
00:32:18,928 --> 00:32:19,971
We don't need to know that.

509
00:32:20,596 --> 00:32:21,848
Oh, okay. Right.

510
00:32:22,098 --> 00:32:24,684
So... so then I started looking
into his shopping profile

511
00:32:24,809 --> 00:32:28,479
focusing on travel, books,
camping gear, stuff like that.

512
00:32:28,813 --> 00:32:31,232
And there were purchases
designed for cold and snow.

513
00:32:31,441 --> 00:32:33,526
But he lives in Colorado.
That's cold and snowy.

514
00:32:33,693 --> 00:32:36,279
Right, but he also bought travel
books for Taos and Albuquerque

515
00:32:36,404 --> 00:32:37,447
both in New Mexico.

516
00:32:37,655 --> 00:32:39,240
Okay, you may be
onto something.

517
00:32:39,365 --> 00:32:40,616
- We'll look into it.
- Wait. That's not all.

518
00:32:40,867 --> 00:32:43,995
On a hunch, I called the new tenant who
moved into Hazel Haibach's apartment.

519
00:32:44,203 --> 00:32:47,123
I asked her if she'd forgotten
anything, needed it mailed. Turn out she did.

520
00:32:47,373 --> 00:32:49,542
The address she gave
was a P.O. box in Santa Fe.

521
00:32:49,876 --> 00:32:50,918
New Mexico.

522
00:32:51,043 --> 00:32:52,170
At the foot of the Sangre de Cristo
mountains.

523
00:32:52,295 --> 00:32:53,379
- Yeah.
- Great.

524
00:32:53,588 --> 00:32:55,423
Get the satellites
looking in the area.

525
00:32:55,548 --> 00:32:57,341
I'll put in a request to get a drone up.

526
00:32:57,467 --> 00:32:59,385
If they are out there,
I think we can find them.

527
00:33:05,057 --> 00:33:07,226
She got away.
That's my girl.

528
00:33:10,605 --> 00:33:12,398
That's all right.
Bet I can find her.

529
00:33:13,191 --> 00:33:14,233
Get back out to the car.

530
00:33:52,396 --> 00:33:53,439
Richard's coming.

531
00:33:53,981 --> 00:33:55,983
Hey, do you think it was by chance
that I picked you up?

532
00:33:56,734 --> 00:33:57,902
That told me
when you escaped.

533
00:33:59,862 --> 00:34:01,280
I was coming for you, stupid.

534
00:34:05,159 --> 00:34:07,954
We think we may have found the place
that Grace Van Pelt is being held.

535
00:34:08,287 --> 00:34:11,123
It's a seasonal cabin up
near the edge of the tree line.

536
00:34:11,707 --> 00:34:14,168
You have evidence of occupation?
Firm evidence?

537
00:34:14,293 --> 00:34:16,170
Smoke coming out of the chimney,
going back six weeks.

538
00:34:17,547 --> 00:34:19,549
Same time Hazel Haibach
left Sacramento.

539
00:34:19,715 --> 00:34:21,217
And there's a gray S.U.V.
parked next to the building.

540
00:34:21,467 --> 00:34:23,553
- It all matches up.
- This must be the place.

541
00:34:24,929 --> 00:34:25,972
Okay.

542
00:34:27,306 --> 00:34:29,016
I'll call the chopper.
We'll be there in an hour.

543
00:34:43,406 --> 00:34:44,448
Pull over and stop.

544
00:34:51,664 --> 00:34:53,207
We're here. Get out.

545
00:34:53,833 --> 00:34:54,875
That's where Grace is?

546
00:34:56,794 --> 00:34:57,837
Get out and see.

547
00:34:58,087 --> 00:35:00,298
And your sister, Hazel, right?
She's there, too?

548
00:35:01,507 --> 00:35:02,550
What?

549
00:35:02,717 --> 00:35:03,759
Well, you didn't think
we knew?

550
00:35:04,302 --> 00:35:05,595
Do we look
that stupid to you?

551
00:35:06,596 --> 00:35:07,722
Shut up
and get out of the car.

552
00:35:10,308 --> 00:35:11,350
No.

553
00:35:13,728 --> 00:35:15,771
Out of the car now.

554
00:35:19,066 --> 00:35:20,109
Think you're a big man,
do you?

555
00:35:20,901 --> 00:35:22,862
You really think I'd let you get away
with what you've done?

556
00:35:26,032 --> 00:35:27,617
I will shoot you
if you don't do what I say.

557
00:35:27,742 --> 00:35:28,784
Believe me.

558
00:35:29,785 --> 00:35:30,828
Go ahead.

559
00:35:31,162 --> 00:35:32,330
I don't think
you have it in you.

560
00:35:42,673 --> 00:35:43,841
Now who looks stupid?

561
00:35:44,717 --> 00:35:47,303
The bullet Rigsby fired next to you
was the only one in the gun.

562
00:35:47,428 --> 00:35:50,306
Not a particularly strong trick,
but it got the job done.

563
00:35:51,599 --> 00:35:52,850
What you're gonna do now
is get your sister

564
00:35:53,100 --> 00:35:55,186
to come out of the house
and put her hands on her head.

565
00:35:59,899 --> 00:36:02,109
Come on. Get out.

566
00:36:12,953 --> 00:36:13,996
Come on.

567
00:36:15,539 --> 00:36:17,083
- Let's go.
- Call out to your sister

568
00:36:17,249 --> 00:36:19,126
and tell her to let Grace go
and come out here.

569
00:36:22,254 --> 00:36:23,297
Hazel?

570
00:36:23,756 --> 00:36:24,799
"Hazel!"

571
00:36:24,924 --> 00:36:25,966
"The police have me."

572
00:36:26,175 --> 00:36:28,010
They say you have
to let the girl go and come out.

573
00:36:29,345 --> 00:36:30,721
"Everything's gonna be fine,
Hazel"

574
00:36:31,597 --> 00:36:32,682
"exactly as your brother says."

575
00:36:33,349 --> 00:36:35,351
No, now you shut up.
No, shut up!

576
00:36:50,991 --> 00:36:52,034
Call out to her again.

577
00:36:53,160 --> 00:36:54,203
Hazel?

578
00:36:57,581 --> 00:37:00,918
I don't know where she is.
Maybe she went out.

579
00:37:01,043 --> 00:37:02,086
Her S.U.V.'s right there.

580
00:37:03,045 --> 00:37:04,088
Hazel!

581
00:37:06,549 --> 00:37:08,342
I don't know where she is.
I don't know.

582
00:37:10,511 --> 00:37:12,138
- That's Grace.
- Rigsby.

583
00:37:12,555 --> 00:37:14,557
- But, Jane, it's Grace.
- Jjust don't panic.

584
00:37:15,558 --> 00:37:16,600
You go.

585
00:37:17,101 --> 00:37:18,144
Be careful.

586
00:37:48,883 --> 00:37:49,925
Stay there.

587
00:37:51,260 --> 00:37:53,679
Grace. It's okay.
Everything's gonna be okay.

588
00:37:54,722 --> 00:37:55,765
I'm gonna
get you out of here.

589
00:37:56,432 --> 00:37:57,475
Where is she?

590
00:37:58,851 --> 00:37:59,894
Behind you!

591
00:38:01,771 --> 00:38:02,813
Nice shot, Hazel!

592
00:38:04,440 --> 00:38:05,483
Don't move.

593
00:38:06,066 --> 00:38:07,318
It's gonna be all right.
I promise.

594
00:38:08,235 --> 00:38:10,070
- Wayne!
- This isn't a trick gun, is it?

595
00:38:10,404 --> 00:38:11,739
- No!
- If I shoot this one

596
00:38:12,114 --> 00:38:13,407
a real bullet will come out,
won't it?

597
00:38:15,951 --> 00:38:16,994
Wayne!

598
00:38:17,620 --> 00:38:18,913
No. No.

599
00:38:19,955 --> 00:38:22,458
No! No, Wayne!

600
00:38:24,168 --> 00:38:25,211
- Wayne?
- Well...

601
00:38:25,711 --> 00:38:26,754
there was at least one.

602
00:38:28,088 --> 00:38:31,008
Let's go have some fun.
Untie her and bring her along.

603
00:38:31,675 --> 00:38:32,718
Come on.

604
00:38:46,565 --> 00:38:47,608
Go on.

605
00:38:49,610 --> 00:38:50,653
Go left.

606
00:38:55,324 --> 00:38:56,367
Left again.

607
00:38:57,576 --> 00:39:00,496
Why so quiet, Mr. Smarty?
Cat got your tongue?

608
00:39:02,456 --> 00:39:04,750
You always have an answer
for everything, usually, don't you?

609
00:39:06,293 --> 00:39:08,379
Go on. Go ahead.
Kneel down.

610
00:39:10,631 --> 00:39:12,007
Right here.
Go ahead.

611
00:39:19,598 --> 00:39:21,517
I thought we could play
a little game.

612
00:39:22,726 --> 00:39:23,769
Like a quiz show.

613
00:39:25,604 --> 00:39:26,647
I'd ask questions...

614
00:39:28,148 --> 00:39:30,484
and you get to keep a finger
for every right answer.

615
00:39:30,734 --> 00:39:32,945
- I'd rather not.
- Okay, first question...

616
00:39:33,821 --> 00:39:34,864
Who's smarter now?

617
00:39:35,197 --> 00:39:36,907
- I don't want to.
- You or me?

618
00:39:37,032 --> 00:39:38,075
I don't... I don't want to.

619
00:39:38,200 --> 00:39:39,743
No answer? Okay.

620
00:39:42,955 --> 00:39:43,998
Wayne!

621
00:39:48,085 --> 00:39:49,962
Wayne. Oh, God, Wayne.

622
00:40:17,740 --> 00:40:19,408
- We need to get to a hospital.
- Yeah.

623
00:40:22,202 --> 00:40:24,246
And then Haibach shot you
a second time?

624
00:40:24,413 --> 00:40:25,956
Yeah. That one hurt.

625
00:40:26,749 --> 00:40:28,542
But you got back up,
disarmed the sister

626
00:40:28,667 --> 00:40:29,710
and stopped Haibach.

627
00:40:30,377 --> 00:40:31,420
Nice work, Wayne.

628
00:40:31,545 --> 00:40:33,005
He said he was gonna save me,
and he did.

629
00:40:34,089 --> 00:40:35,716
You do realize you got shot
with your own gun.

630
00:40:36,050 --> 00:40:38,385
Oh, please, Cho, no jokes.
It hurts when I laugh.

631
00:40:38,594 --> 00:40:40,554
No, I'm just saying, if you tell
that story in the future

632
00:40:40,679 --> 00:40:41,847
you might want to leave
that part out.

633
00:40:41,972 --> 00:40:43,474
Seriously, I'm gonna split a stitch.

634
00:40:45,476 --> 00:40:46,936
We should go,
let you get some rest.

635
00:40:48,604 --> 00:40:50,940
I don't know what we would have
done if we'd lost you.

636
00:40:51,357 --> 00:40:52,608
I knew you guys would come.

637
00:40:53,567 --> 00:40:54,610
Bye.

638
00:40:59,782 --> 00:41:02,034
You two take very good care
of each other.

639
00:41:06,830 --> 00:41:07,873
Didn't mean to interrupt.

640
00:41:07,998 --> 00:41:10,376
Oh, we were, uh...
Just leaving.

641
00:41:11,168 --> 00:41:12,211
Bye.

642
00:41:16,340 --> 00:41:18,342
I wanted to come by and see
how you're doing.

643
00:41:18,801 --> 00:41:19,843
Thank you.

644
00:41:20,052 --> 00:41:22,638
And to let you know that you
impressed the hell out of us.

645
00:41:23,222 --> 00:41:24,765
Not too many people
can do what you did.

646
00:41:25,933 --> 00:41:27,643
Thank you. Really.

647
00:41:28,227 --> 00:41:29,561
We're just glad
that you're both okay.

648
00:41:30,187 --> 00:41:31,230
Yeah.

649
00:41:32,898 --> 00:41:33,941
Yeah.

650
00:41:35,317 --> 00:41:39,571
And if you two ever think about
getting back to our side of the business

651
00:41:40,280 --> 00:41:41,323
give me a call.

652
00:41:42,658 --> 00:41:43,701
I don't think so.

653
00:41:44,660 --> 00:41:46,120
Civilian life, here we come.

654
00:41:47,079 --> 00:41:48,122
Well, that's too bad.

655
00:41:49,039 --> 00:41:50,582
Anyhow, the offer's still open.

656
00:41:51,250 --> 00:41:52,292
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

657
00:41:52,459 --> 00:41:53,502
- Take care.
- Bye.

658
00:41:55,504 --> 00:41:56,964
Okay. I'm gonna head out, too.

659
00:41:57,881 --> 00:42:00,634
Oh, don't go yet, buddy.
Got lunch coming up.

660
00:42:01,427 --> 00:42:02,469
I can get you your own.

661
00:42:03,345 --> 00:42:04,388
Hospital lunch?

662
00:42:04,513 --> 00:42:08,183
It's really not that bad.
They got cherry cobbler.

663
00:42:13,063 --> 00:42:15,149
I was really angry
at you for doing what you did

664
00:42:15,315 --> 00:42:16,734
but then I thought better of it.

665
00:42:16,859 --> 00:42:19,153
It was a stupid idea,
but, hey, it worked.

666
00:42:19,278 --> 00:42:21,363
Whoa. Stupid?
Not necessarily stupid.

667
00:42:21,488 --> 00:42:22,990
Simple. Not stupid.

668
00:42:23,115 --> 00:42:24,199
But I am still angry at you

669
00:42:24,324 --> 00:42:25,659
for not telling me
what you were gonna do.

670
00:42:25,868 --> 00:42:26,910
I thought you'd gone nuts.

671
00:42:27,036 --> 00:42:29,496
Oh, come on, please. It's not like I haven't
abducted people before.

672
00:42:29,830 --> 00:42:31,665
It's not funny.
I was really scared.

673
00:42:32,624 --> 00:42:34,001
- I'm sorry.
- No, you're not.

674
00:42:34,710 --> 00:42:36,837
I can tell when
you're not being sincere now.

675
00:42:37,046 --> 00:42:39,006
Well, clearly, you can't,
because I am sorry.

676
00:42:39,131 --> 00:42:41,008
I can tell just by looking
at you, okay?

677
00:42:41,133 --> 00:42:42,593
But you can't see
what I'm feeling.

